cat > docs/architecture.md <<'EOF'
# LLM Inference Topology

## Purpose

This project models an LLM inference system
as an operational topology.

It does not claim to reproduce the internal
Transformer computation.

Instead, it provides a framework for
representing:

1. input;
2. context;
3. policy/control;
4. model inference;
5. compute substrate;
6. output validation;
7. application rendering.

## Layer model

L4  Application / Interface
        |
L3  Context / Orchestration
        |
L2  Policy / Control
        |
L1  Model Inference
        |
L0  Compute Substrate

## Formal pipeline

I(X) -> intent representation

C(I) -> contextual state

P(C) -> policy/control state

M(P) -> model inference

V(M) -> validation

O(V) -> output

Complete abstraction:

O = V(M(P(C(I(X)))))

This is a software-pipeline abstraction.
It is not a literal representation of every
internal Transformer operation.

## Experimental objective

Measure:

- latency;
- throughput;
- token counts;
- context size;
- validation failures;
- routing decisions;
- cache behavior;
- model/provider differences;
- topology changes.

## Scope boundary

The project does not currently implement:

- a Transformer;
- GPU kernels;
- a new inference engine;
- RLHF;
- model training.

External inference systems can be used as
backends for experiments.
EOF

